{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1488445-stasis-resistance","id":1488445,"title":"Stasis Resistance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-30T03:26:05-07:00","id":1488445,"title":"Stasis Resistance","content":"So, if say a changeling use Winter 5 power Stasis against a vampire, would he add his Fortitude to his Stamina in order to resist the power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T15:08:55-07:00","id":1488497,"title":"","content":"Does anybody have any idea? I have the impression that yes the cainite should add his Fortitude to his Stamina in order to resist being frozen, but one friend thinks it shouldn't add...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T18:34:05-07:00","id":1488635,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to say no- Fortitude helps you soak damage, not make other Stamina rolls. Given that Changelings typically don't have super high Stamina either (max of 5 for most Kith, other than, say, Satyrs, for example), and that vampires can increase Stamina in other ways (spending blood, Elemental Mastery), it seems unfair to give Fortitude more power here, even though normally, I would admit Fortitude is somewhat weak.<br /> <br /> Consider the difficulty of using the Art on a vampire in the first place, if it's a PC Changeling, I wouldn't make it harder for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T19:12:52-07:00","id":1488637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1488445-stasis-resistance?p=1488635#post1488635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to say no- Fortitude helps you soak damage, not make other Stamina rolls. Given that Changelings typically don't have super high Stamina either (max of 5 for most Kith, other than, say, Satyrs, for example), and that vampires can increase Stamina in other ways (spending blood, Elemental Mastery), it seems unfair to give Fortitude more power here, even though normally, I would admit Fortitude is somewhat weak.<br /> <br /> Consider the difficulty of using the Art on a vampire in the first place, if it's a PC Changeling, I wouldn't make it harder for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The changeling in the case is an antagonist, I'm sincerely in doubt about it. The group is going to face a powerful changeling and I'm thinking ahead because most of the group has Fortitude. I'm more inclined to say no now after your answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T19:25:56-07:00","id":1488639,"title":"","content":"Yeah, considering how fragile Changelings can be, there's not much point in giving your players more advantages. They can't soak lethal with Stamina, they have to invoke the Wyrd to use any chimerical armor. Dragon's Ire increases damage diffs by 2, but as I found out (just tonight, in fact), that's not a guarantee of anything, lol. But just to affect the Kindred, you have to either Enchant them or Invoke the Wyrd (1 Glamour, 1 Willpower, roll Glamour diff of the local Banality). Unless you have Art or Actor Affinity, your attempt is Winter+Actor diff 8, and if you decide any of the vampires have a Banality of 7 or more, the diff is increased by another 1. You can lower the diff with Bunks, but those take turns you probably don't have if you have any Celerity fiends in the party.<br /> <br /> Because of course, just like all other Arts, Wayfare, which grants extra actions, has to be activated as an action in advance. So anything like a combat is probably going to end up with a squished Fae. <br /> <br /> Unless, of course, you just use the fact that Changelings are able to go about in the day time and you can't tell they aren't mortals without Auspex or Mytherceria to your advantage, lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T19:36:14-07:00","id":1488642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1488445-stasis-resistance?p=1488639#post1488639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, considering how fragile Changelings can be, there's not much point in giving your players more advantages. They can't soak lethal with Stamina, they have to invoke the Wyrd to use any chimerical armor. Dragon's Ire increases damage diffs by 2, but as I found out (just tonight, in fact), that's not a guarantee of anything, lol. But just to affect the Kindred, you have to either Enchant them or Invoke the Wyrd (1 Glamour, 1 Willpower, roll Glamour diff of the local Banality). Unless you have Art or Actor Affinity, your attempt is Winter+Actor diff 8, and if you decide any of the vampires have a Banality of 7 or more, the diff is increased by another 1. You can lower the diff with Bunks, but those take turns you probably don't have if you have any Celerity fiends in the party.<br /> <br /> Because of course, just like all other Arts, Wayfare, which grants extra actions, has to be activated as an action in advance. So anything like a combat is probably going to end up with a squished Fae.<br /> <br /> Unless, of course, you just use the fact that Changelings are able to go about in the day time and you can't tell they aren't mortals without Auspex or Mytherceria to your advantage, lol.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Changeling is a very powerful one and has some allies, in fact, the group only has a chance in my opinion because they have a powerful NPC with them. They're going to attack her in her Freehold. It's definitely not going to be easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T19:38:02-07:00","id":1488643,"title":"","content":"Oh and I forgot to mention, the game is set in 1500, so things are much easier for the Changelings. Banality isn't anywhere as high as today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T01:41:52-07:00","id":1488952,"title":"","content":"&quot;System: A character\u2019s Fortitude rating adds to all<br /> her Stamina-based dice pools, including her soak rating<br /> for bashing and lethal damage. A vampire may use her<br /> Fortitude dice as a soak pool against aggravated wounds,<br /> which vampires typically have no recourse against. Once<br /> per turn, she may spend a blood point to automatically<br /> soak her Fortitude in damage, instead of adding it to her<br /> Stamina. This can be used to soak aggravated damage as<br /> well, but not damage from fire or sunlight&quot;<br /> <br /> DaV20 pg 221<br /> <br /> So yes, you would add fortitude to the pool<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25428-ebtard","name":"Ebtard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T07:34:44-07:00","id":1488974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1488445-stasis-resistance?p=1488635#post1488635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to say no- Fortitude helps you soak damage, not make other Stamina rolls. Given that Changelings typically don't have super high Stamina either (max of 5 for most Kith, other than, say, Satyrs, for example), and that vampires can increase Stamina in other ways (spending blood, Elemental Mastery), it seems unfair to give Fortitude more power here, even though normally, I would admit Fortitude is somewhat weak.<br /> <br /> Consider the difficulty of using the Art on a vampire in the first place, if it's a PC Changeling, I wouldn't make it harder for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont agree with that. Crossovers are NOT balanced. If a neonate vampire cross a werewolf, the werewolf is not supposed to lose his claws because &quot;it's unfair&quot;. A Mage is essentially a fragile human, so if said Mage doesnt have tons of Hit Marks or the Armor of Titans, a neonate Brujah vampire will kill him; on the other hand, a Mage with several fetishes and artefacts and perma effects will remove the vampire's soul from it's body, place it in a jar and do unholy experiments with both soul and body for pretty much all the eternity in some bizarre alien world.<br /> <br /> It's just the way that it is. So, if it causes damage, Fortitude can soak.<br /> <br /> Now, Changellings do have other INSANELY powerful capabilities; just looking at Cantrips and Arts is limiting too much what their full range of possibilities really are.<br /> <br /> First of all, have the villain fight in his own &quot;turf&quot;. The bold vampires track the damn Fae-alien thing to his &quot;haven&quot; and... End up in the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> In there, the vamps are his bit***. More than simply using their arts, the &quot;Fair Folk&quot; have access to basically unlimited supplies of &quot;trans-dimensional&quot; bizarre alien Chimerae. So, is the Changelling too &quot;weak&quot; for your tastes?<br /> <br /> Well, maybe he is... But his Dragon best pal is another story...<br /> <br /> Or, the vamps may try their luck against a Xenomorph Chimerae, or perhaps a swarm of Zergs... or a centaur, cyclops, or perhaps the giant world eater worm Apophis... How about they track the Changelling down, only to end up facing the mountain sized wolf Fenrir?<br /> <br /> Or, instead of a &quot;living&quot; Chimerae, perhaps the Fae have the flamming sword of the Gabriel Archangel, a true &quot;demonslayer&quot; sword (which would cut vampires like hot knife on butter), or Excalibur, or Thor's hammer Mjolnir, or Hermes sandals...<br /> <br /> The Chimerae the Changelling have at his disposal can be as powerful as you'd like. Just adjust them to the &quot;challenge level&quot; you'd like (after all, using Excallibur or summoning Apophis against neonates would be too much)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T16:03:43-07:00","id":1489023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1488445-stasis-resistance?p=1488974#post1488974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont agree with that. Crossovers are NOT balanced. If a neonate vampire cross a werewolf, the werewolf is not supposed to lose his claws because &quot;it's unfair&quot;. A Mage is essentially a fragile human, so if said Mage doesnt have tons of Hit Marks or the Armor of Titans, a neonate Brujah vampire will kill him; on the other hand, a Mage with several fetishes and artefacts and perma effects will remove the vampire's soul from it's body, place it in a jar and do unholy experiments with both soul and body for pretty much all the eternity in some bizarre alien world.<br /> <br /> It's just the way that it is. So, if it causes damage, Fortitude can soak.<br /> <br /> Now, Changellings do have other INSANELY powerful capabilities; just looking at Cantrips and Arts is limiting too much what their full range of possibilities really are.<br /> <br /> First of all, have the villain fight in his own &quot;turf&quot;. The bold vampires track the damn Fae-alien thing to his &quot;haven&quot; and... End up in the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> In there, the vamps are his bit***. More than simply using their arts, the &quot;Fair Folk&quot; have access to basically unlimited supplies of &quot;trans-dimensional&quot; bizarre alien Chimerae. So, is the Changelling too &quot;weak&quot; for your tastes?<br /> <br /> Well, maybe he is... But his Dragon best pal is another story...<br /> <br /> Or, the vamps may try their luck against a Xenomorph Chimerae, or perhaps a swarm of Zergs... or a centaur, cyclops, or perhaps the giant world eater worm Apophis... How about they track the Changelling down, only to end up facing the mountain sized wolf Fenrir?<br /> <br /> Or, instead of a &quot;living&quot; Chimerae, perhaps the Fae have the flamming sword of the Gabriel Archangel, a true &quot;demonslayer&quot; sword (which would cut vampires like hot knife on butter), or Excalibur, or Thor's hammer Mjolnir, or Hermes sandals...<br /> <br /> The Chimerae the Changelling have at his disposal can be as powerful as you'd like. Just adjust them to the &quot;challenge level&quot; you'd like (after all, using Excallibur or summoning Apophis against neonates would be too much)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes pretty much this. In the WoD it's NEVER that simple to anticipate the result in a conflict between different splats, to be fair not even in the same splat, as a neonate armed with a powerful weapon/fetich or whatever could easily kill an elder and so on, this, besides the obvious advantages in the field, e.g. attacking in number, unexpected circumstances etc. Changelings have access to very op powers, just look at Dragon's Ire's Holy Strike that has one of the highest potential damage in the entire WoD and it's just a level 4 in the Art and that could cause insane 30 damage lol<br /> <br /> The thing is the Changelling in question is a very powerful one and the PCs want to surprise her, by attacking her own freehold with the help of a powerful NPC. They are fully aware of the risks, they even joked last session that theyre gong to bring blank character's sheets because they fear they'll be destroyed. By the way they're not neonates, it's an elder chronicle set in the Renaissance. My question was more because I'm sincerely in doubt about which one is the best option, systematically talking. Fortitude is added to the resistance against Mastery of the Mortal Shell's Path of Thaumaturgy and that's one of the reasons I was (and I'm still btw) in doubt if I should let it add dice to their resistance or not. The system isn't very clear and there isn't an &quot;official&quot; answer, so I need to decide what I think is best. In any case, it's important because it sets a precedent in other similar cases, so I wanted different opinions here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T16:31:49-07:00","id":1489027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1488445-stasis-resistance?p=1489023#post1489023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes pretty much this. In the WoD it's NEVER that simple to anticipate the result in a conflict between different splats, to be fair not even in the same splat, as a neonate armed with a powerful weapon/fetich or whatever could easily kill an elder and so on, this, besides the obvious advantages in the field, e.g. attacking in number, unexpected circumstances etc. Changelings have access to very op powers, just look at Dragon's Ire's Holy Strike that has one of the highest potential damage in the entire WoD and it's just a level 4 in the Art and that could cause insane 30 damage lol<br /> <br /> The thing is the Changelling in question is a very powerful one and the PCs want to surprise her, by attacking her own freehold with the help of a powerful NPC. They are fully aware of the risks, they even joked last session that theyre gong to bring blank character's sheets because they fear they'll be destroyed. By the way they're not neonates, it's an elder chronicle set in the Renaissance. My question was more because I'm sincerely in doubt about which one is the best option, systematically talking. Fortitude is added to the resistance against Mastery of the Mortal Shell's Path of Thaumaturgy and that's one of the reasons I was (and I'm still btw) in doubt if I should let it add dice to their resistance or not. The system isn't very clear and there isn't an &amp;quot;official&amp;quot; answer, so I need to decide what I think is best. In any case, it's important because it sets a precedent in other similar cases, so I wanted different opinions here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im in the opinion that &quot;you get what you paid for&quot;. If it causes damage, Fortitude can soak. The end.<br /> <br /> As for attacking a Fae in their own freehold... Good luck with that. A Mage I would say it have a <i>slight</i> better chance. As for a vampire... I hope they enjoy spending a few decades in the Dreaming and coming back mad (if ever). That's just one of the possibilities. Getting eaten by a dragon is another. Or becoming the next meal of Apophis... Anyway, I'll trust your balancing skills as a ST.<br /> <br /> Regardless, Fortitude ALWAYS soak, unless there's some sort of weird magic that can completely disable the discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T03:49:31-07:00","id":1489083,"title":"","content":"Except Stasis doesn't inflict damage. It causes the target to be frozen for up to a year, resisted by a Stamina roll. And it does come down to which version of Fortitude you use for your games- the V20 version only affects soak, not other Stamina rolls. Herr Meister didn't say in their OP that they were using the Dark Ages rules- the V20 Fortitude specifies it only adds to Stamina to soak damage (or it can be used alone to soak aggravated damage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}